      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now let me check the working directory for compile.sh and understand the test structure better.Now I have a clear picture of the test. I'll write an improved version that:\n- Removes all unused imports and constants\n- Simplifies the large helper methods to only what's needed\n- Makes the test method's intent clearThe improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes all unused imports and constants, eliminates the complex delegation chain (`doReplace` → `doTestReplace`) by inlining the logic directly into the test method, adds a class-level Javadoc explaining the three scenarios under test, and uses named constants (`TEMPLATE`/`EXPECTED`) with inline comments that describe exactly what each variable substitution does."
